    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Suno is a for-profit startup founded in 2022 and headquartered in Cambridge, MA, USA. The company describes itself as an AI music generator that lets users create original music for free in seconds. Its website says users can make songs, remix tracks, make beats, and share music, and it presents Suno Studio as a web-based generative audio workstation that combines traditional DAW functionality with AI-powered music creation.\n\nThe company's product, Suno, is listed in the Voice & Audio category with a note on music generation and IP provenance. Suno's site describes paid plans: a Pro plan with 500 songs a month, access to v5.5, commercial use rights, priority generation, a Song Editor, stem separation, and audio uploads up to 8 minutes; and a Premier plan with 2,000 songs a month, Suno Studio, a multitrack editor, MIDI export, Persona Voices, and early access to new features.\n\nTen court cases name Suno, Inc., including UMG Recordings, Sony Music et al. v. Suno, Inc. in the U.S. District Court for the District of Massachusetts, and other cases in federal district courts in California, Texas, New York, and Illinois.",
